{"skill":{"slug":"dreaming","displayName":"Dreaming"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1771688819877,"changelog":"- Added initial state tracking file: `data/dream-state.json`.\n- The skill can now persist nightly dream counts and related state.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4792,"sha256":"f3e470f1cec49b1ceff59f3f7bb26be1d4a651f12ad29ef855f36cb13041c2a2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"data/dream-state.json","size":106,"sha256":"13ad354b2388fd95e723ff57a48034151fd52653bd79b275813e66eb00341152","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/should-dream.sh","size":4061,"sha256":"f21c9ed2a4851860994cdef299bf1eba0f21ef414d52e9fe582a6239c06127c0","contentType":"application/x-shellscript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1825,"sha256":"37ba555a66aaba30079bee0a859d88ef1da51b7529e1ef00e17e4b768aa42840","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789033194731,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0ef52daade1c910b5a45674cb6319df39c138c8569f827cf9d87d0b8c3721a20","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0ef52daade1c910b5a45674cb6319df39c138c8569f827cf9d87d0b8c3721a20","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: dreaming\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThe skill 'dreaming' is designed for creative exploration during quiet hours, writing outputs to designated files within its workspace. It uses standard binaries (`jq`, `python3`) for state management and random chance calculation. All file operations are confined to the skill's `data/` and `memory/` directories. The `SKILL.md` instructions guide the agent to parse a `category:prompt` string and write a thoughtful exploration, which aligns with its stated purpose and does not contain any instructions for malicious actions like data exfiltration, unauthorized command execution, or prompt injection with harmful objectives. The use of `jq` with `--arg` and `--argjson` for state updates, and `jq -r` for reading, appears robust against injection. The `python3 -c` command is also not vulnerable to shell injection from the `$DREAM_CHANCE` variable.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161343190},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":41,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789033194731},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly coherent and disclosed, but its local state configuration can be abused to execute arbitrary Python code if the state file is modified.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The shell script reads dreamChance from data/dream-state.json and interpolates it directly into python3 -c source text, so a modified state file can turn a numeric configuration field into local code execution.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package consists of a markdown skill, one shell script, and a JSON state file, with disclosed jq and python3 requirements; no remote install, dependency download, hook, or service setup was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Autonomous heartbeat use and persistent dream writing are disclosed, including default quiet hours and output paths, but users should treat this as an opt-in background behavior because it can create reflective files without a task-specific prompt.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Persistence is limited to documented workspace files under data/ and memory/dreams, with no system-level persistence or credential access observed, but the generated reflections may contain sensitive context if enabled broadly.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, quiet-hours creative output, matches the artifact: the script gates whether a dream should occur, selects a topic, and the skill instructs the agent to write the dream file for later review.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an opt-in heartbeat routine that writes reflective notes to the workspace. Before enabling it, fix or constrain dreamChance handling, keep data/dream-state.json writable only by trusted components, and avoid letting the agent store sensitive private or client information in dream files.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: artifact/scripts/should-dream.sh uses the unvalidated dreamChance value inside python3 -c, which is unnecessary for the skill purpose and creates a local code-execution path if the state file is attacker-controlled or corrupted.\n[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the artifact explicitly says the script is a gate and that the agent, not the script, writes memory/dreams/YYYY-MM-DD.md, so this is not a supported description-to-behavior mismatch.\n[SQP-1] expected: The quiet-hours heartbeat activation is broad but disclosed and user-installed via HEARTBEAT.md; it is a governance consideration rather than hidden behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Persistent dream files are part of the stated function and are disclosed in the description and directories-written section, though users should configure retention and sensitivity expectations before enabling it.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789033194731}}}}}